1. **`getDeclaredConstructor()`**: This method is called on a `Class` object and returns a `Constructor` object that represents a declared constructor of the class. Unlike `getConstructor()`, which only returns public constructors, `getDeclaredConstructor()` can return any constructor (public, protected, default, or private) defined in the class.

